    <briefdescription>
<para>Sealed blob — data bound to the current TEE measurement. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Unsealing will fail if the enclave measurement changes (e.g. after a software update), providing &quot;measured-boot&quot; style binding.</para>
<para>In software-fallback mode the blob is AES-256-GCM encrypted with a process-lifetime key derived from OpenSSL RAND_bytes; it will NOT survive process restart. Real TDX/SEV implementations should persist measurement-bound key material through a remote KMS. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
